    "_model_pin_comment": "PLAN-163 T1.1 contingency (ADR-181 \u00a7Contingency) \u2014 session-default pin. CC 2.1.220 honors the top-level settings key \"model\" (zod: E.string().optional(); describe \"Override the default model used by Claude Code\"; source at 2.1.220 binary offset 226819212, sha256 8addc857..., between \"permissions\" and \"fallbackModel\"). Pinned to claude-opus-5 so that adding claude-sonnet-5 to availableModels cannot silently flip the session default to the 2.1.220 sonnet-5 tier-default (enforceAvailableModels stops redirecting once sonnet-5 is allowed). ADOPTER NOTE: a fresh install therefore inherits claude-opus-5 as the session default (Opus pricing $5/$25 per MTok). If that is not desired for your workload, override the value here (e.g. \"claude-sonnet-5\" or your tier default) or set env ANTHROPIC_MODEL / pass CLI --model per-session; the pinned value MUST stay a member of availableModels below or enforceAvailableModels rejects it. Keep this key mirrored with .claude/settings.json in the framework repo (test_session_default_pin).",
    "model": "claude-opus-5",
    "availableModels": [
        "claude-opus-4-8",
        "claude-fable-5",
        "claude-sonnet-4-6",
        "claude-haiku-4-5",
        "claude-opus-5",
        "claude-sonnet-5",
        "claude-fable-5-1"
    ],
    "fallbackModel": [
        "claude-opus-5"
    ],
    "_posture_keys_comment": "PLAN-163 T5.3/OQ5 \u2014 fail-closed posture keys (CC >=2.1.220). Key (1) permissions.defaultMode ships LIVE below (see _default_mode_arbitration_comment); the REMAINING keys ship COMMENTED for adopters. Dogfood status (2026-08-03): the framework repo enables workflowSizeGuideline and the sandbox keys; disableAutoMode was REMOVED from the dogfood settings by Owner decision (ceremony [SENT-PLAN165]) \u2014 beyond the documented no-mid-session-escalation effect it also strips 'auto' from the operator's native shift+tab mode cycle, and choosing the session mode is the operator's call, not the framework's. Adopters may still opt in. To adopt, add the keys literally: (2) top-level \"disableAutoMode\": \"disable\" \u2014 string enum whose sole value is 'disable' (the 2.1.220 schema rejects a boolean and SKIPS THE WHOLE settings file on mismatch \u2014 S286 live-fire); prevents automatic permission-mode escalation mid-session. (3) top-level \"workflowSizeGuideline\": <per your workflow scale; advisory sizing guideline for Workflow-tool fan-outs>. (4) \"sandbox\": { \"network\": { \"strictAllowlist\": true } } \u2014 tightens allowedDomains matching to the strict form. (5) \"sandbox\": { \"filesystem\": { \"disabled\": false } } \u2014 keeps filesystem confinement armed when the sandbox is enabled (true would fail-OPEN the FS layer). All keys are independent and additive; rollback is deleting the key. NEW-EVENT hook registrations (DirectoryAdded/Notification) are deliberately NOT in this template yet \u2014 T3.4 version-floor feature gate (upgrade.sh, default OFF), ADR-183 residual (e); this template stays at 45 registrations until the floor probe is recorded. This block is documentation only \u2014 underscore-prefixed keys are ignored by the harness.",
    "_default_mode_arbitration_comment": "PLAN-163 T3.5/T5.3 ARBITRATION (CEO S284, ADR-183): permissions.defaultMode='manual' is a LIVE key in this template, not a commented posture option. Rationale: install.sh copies this file verbatim on a fresh install, and the U1 post-install oracle (test_upgrade_settings_migration.py TestU1TemplateParity) asserts the template already carries the T5.4 NEW baseline (defaultMode='manual', the 2.1.2xx rename of the ask-first permission mode \u2014 every non-allowlisted tool call prompts) \u2014 a commented-only defaultMode would red U1 and ship fresh installs on the OLD 'default' posture. Rollback: delete the defaultMode key (single-line revert; no hook consumes it \u2014 harness-level only).",
    "_night_mode_deny_surface_comment": "PLAN-165 P1-corrected (D2 + round-2 findings NM-01/NM-03 + codex CX-1) \u2014 under defaultMode=acceptEdits a tool Edit/Write is auto-accepted, so every file that can DECIDE the next session's posture is deny-listed: (1) .claude/settings.local.json, the per-machine overlay (gitignored) that decides the NEXT session's permission posture; (2) .claude/state/night-mode.json, the night-mode marker/snapshot whose prev_value is restored into the overlay by night-mode off \u2014 a posture write BY PROXY (NM-01); (3) .claude/scripts/night-mode.py, the single sanctioned writer itself (NM-03). HONEST SCOPE (CX-1): per-TOOL deny entries close only the Edit/Write rail; the Bash rail is closed by _CANONICAL_GUARDS in check_canonical_edit.py (all three paths listed) + kernel-tier listing of the two state files. The script writes as a PROCESS, never via the Edit/Write tools, so the deny costs no legitimate path. The Write() twins were REMOVED in S292: the current harness (>=2.1.216) does NOT consult Write(path) rules in its file-permission check (the CLI emits an active warning for such rules) and the Edit(path) entries cover ALL file-editing tools \u2014 the same class PLAN-161 C1 removed from the credential-read baseline; the old-CLI residual documented there is now accepted for the posture files too, with the real defense on the _CANONICAL_GUARDS/kernel rails (CX-1). Mirrors .claude/settings.json in the framework repo (dogfood parity) \u2014 the three entries are byte-identical in both files.",
    "permissions": {
        "defaultMode": "manual",
        "deny": [
            "Bash(git push --force*)",
            "Edit(PROTOCOL.md)",
            "Edit(.claude/settings.json)",
            "Edit(SPEC/**)",
            "Edit(.claude/settings.local.json)",
            "Edit(.claude/state/night-mode.json)",
