   161	## CI gates (Sprint 3 Item B)
   162	
   163	The framework ships with two distinct floor gates on benchmark scores:
   164	
   165	| Gate | Threshold | Source | Effect |
   166	|------|-----------|--------|--------|
   167	| **CRITICAL floor** | overall score < 0.4 | `scoring.health_thresholds.critical` in benchmark YAML | `run-skill-benchmark.py` exits 1. CI fails. Always enforced — no opt-out. |
   168	| **Absolute floor** | overall score < 0.6 | `--floor 0.6` CLI flag (passed by `benchmarks.yml`) | Same exit code (rc=1). CI fails. Can be tuned per-environment. |
   169	
   170	Both gates share exit code 1 by design (debate round 1 consensus
   171	R-DEV1): having separate exit codes for "CRITICAL" vs "absolute floor"
   172	fragments CI error handling without buying clarity. Distinguish via
